From 82ab28e84a4de238b04fab20ef7e46c98fa9a68c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alp Lab AB <contact@alplab.ai>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 05:42:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] media: i2c: imx335: add 2-lane support and a 10-bit
 binned mode

The 6.1 driver only accepts four CSI-2 data lanes and one mode,
2592x1940 SRGGB12_1X12. The InnoMaker IMX335 module routes two lanes.

Read the lane count (2 or 4) from the endpoint data-lanes and program
LANEMODE accordingly, as mainline does. Move the 24 MHz
INCK PLL registers into the 1188 Mbps/lane MIPI data rate table, also
writing SYSMODE and the MIPI output timing block (0x3a18-0x3a28), which
the 6.1 driver left at their reset values.

Add a second mode, 1296x972 SRGGB10_1X10 (2x2 binned), and select the
12/10-bit AD, MIPI data width and ADBIT1 registers per mode. The mode
register lists also restore the registers the other mode changes, so
switching modes on a running device is safe. The binned list uses
HNUM 0x0a08 and Y_OUT_SIZE 0x03cc: the sensor otherwise transmits
1308x984 into a 1296x972 buffer.

Derive V4L2_CID_PIXEL_RATE from link frequency, lane count and bits per
pixel instead of the fixed 396 MHz. The RZ/G2L CSI-2 receiver sets its
D-PHY rate from pixel rate * bpp / lanes, so 2 lanes at 10 bit must
report 237.6 MHz to land on 1188 Mbps/lane. The link frequency stays
594 MHz for both lane counts.

Hide modes that do not fit the link at the connected lane count: 2592x1940
12-bit needs 13.1 us per line on 2 lanes against the 7.41 us line period
at the default HMAX, so with 2 lanes enum_mbus_code, enum_frame_size and
set_fmt only offer the binned mode, which is also the default. The binned
hblank is 464 so its line time stays 7.41 us at the 237.6 MHz pixel rate.

Reject set_fmt on a streaming sensor and size the exposure range per
mode (shutter minimum is 17 lines when binned).

Upstream-Status: Pending [2-lane/10-bit exists upstream with a different
register split; this is a 6.1 backport for the Renesas BSP]

Signed-off-by: Alp Lab AB <contact@alplab.ai>
